# IslandIntakeStale and IslandIntakeClaimsUnread (homelab#3580) + IslandIntakeUnruledOld (homelab#3837) + IntakeExperimentOverdue and IntakeExperimentReadStale (homelab#3604), lifted VERBATIM out of prometheusrule.yaml (comments stripped — the manifest is its
# one home) — the rules file that island-intake.promtool-test loads. Not a manifest and not applied to
# anything: `promtool test rules` needs upstream-format rules (top-level `groups:`), and a
# PrometheusRule keeps them under `.spec`. Named .promtool-rules rather than .yaml on purpose —
# manifest-lint kubeconforms EVERY *.yaml under argocd/resources.
#
# The island intake's alerts, their OWN file, for the same reason DeepDigStale has one (deep-dig.promtool-
# rules' header): the restart-gap contract is a DIFFERENCE-shaped behaviour worth its own fixture.
#
# ⚠ Drift-pinned by `devbox run prometheus-rules-lint`'s bidirectional CR↔copy pin — re-copy after
# editing the alert:
#
#   yq -o=json '{"groups": [{"name": "agent-runs", "rules": [.spec.groups[].rules[] | select(.alert == "IslandIntakeStale" or .alert == "IslandIntakeUnruledOld" or .alert == "IslandIntakeClaimsUnread" or .alert == "IntakeExperimentOverdue" or .alert == "IntakeExperimentReadStale")]}]}' argocd/resources/pushgateway/prometheusrule.yaml | yq -P '.'
groups:
  - name: agent-runs
    rules:
      - alert: IslandIntakeStale
        expr: ((time() - max by (island) (max_over_time(island_intake_last_run_timestamp_seconds[8d]))) > 2 * 86400) and on (island) (max by (island) (max_over_time(island_intake_listed_timestamp_seconds[8d])) == on () group_left () max(max_over_time(island_intake_listed_timestamp_seconds[8d])))
        for: 6h
        labels:
          severity: warning
          platform_machinery: "true"
          triage: none
        annotations:
          summary: Island intake has not run for the {{ $labels.island }} island in >2 days — its findings, issues and waits are not being admitted
          description: 'The daily 05:00Z island-intake CronWorkflow (ns agent-coordinator) holds a sitting per island; the {{ $labels.island }} island''s has not pushed a run in over 2 days. Its dig findings, unruled issues and waits stay unread until it does. Check: argo -n agent-coordinator cron get island-intake and the newest island-intake-* workflow (the `sitting` step of that island, or a walk that ended before reaching it); re-fire that island via: argo -n agent-coordinator submit --from cronworkflow/island-intake -p island={{ $labels.island }}. Brief: islands/intake/rules/intake.md; the island list: islands/intake/scripts/intake-select.sh --list-islands.'
      - alert: IslandIntakeUnruledOld
        expr: max by (island) (island_intake_oldest_unruled_age_seconds) > 72 * 3600
        for: 1h
        labels:
          severity: warning
          triage: dig
        annotations:
          summary: The {{ $labels.island }} island's oldest unruled issue was {{ $value | humanizeDuration }} old at its last intake sitting — above the KPI target (72 h from filing to a ruling)
          description: 'island_intake_oldest_unruled_age_seconds{island="{{ $labels.island }}"} is {{ $value | humanizeDuration }} (target: at most 72 h). The daily 05:00Z island-intake CronWorkflow (ns agent-coordinator) pushes it from every sitting that read its selection: the age of the oldest issue of the island that carried no agent/* label and no intake: ruling when the sitting was offered it (0 when none). An issue is offered at the first daily sitting after it is 24 h old, so a value above 72 h means sittings ran and left it unruled, or did not run. Check: (1) bash islands/intake/scripts/intake-select.sh --island {{ $labels.island }} names the unruled issues and their ages; (2) the island''s receipts under s3://agent-transcripts/homelab/intake-<island>-<day>/ for an INTAKE-RULED line on that issue (deferred, or none: a sitting that ended before its writes); (3) IslandIntakeStale for a sitting that did not run. The KPI and its target are named in islands/intake/README.md §Consumer contracts.'
      - alert: IslandIntakeClaimsUnread
        expr: max(island_intake_claims_read_ok) == 0
        for: 2d
        labels:
          severity: warning
          platform_machinery: "true"
          triage: none
        annotations:
          summary: Island intake has not read the AgentStack claims for 2 days — no stack island is getting a sitting
          description: 'The daily 05:00Z island-intake CronWorkflow (ns agent-coordinator) reads the live AgentStack claims in its list step to find the stack islands (repos[].intake.facts). That read has failed or answered no claim on every run for 2 days: the platform islands are still walked, every stack island is skipped. Check the `islands` step''s log of the newest island-intake-* workflow (the line `island-intake: claims read FAILED — stack islands not walked` and the one after it), and: kubectl auth can-i list agentstacks.platform.teststuff.net --as=system:serviceaccount:agent-coordinator:island-intake (the rule is on ClusterRole island-intake-read, agents/coordinator/rbac.yaml). Reader: islands/intake/scripts/claims-read.sh.'
      - alert: IntakeExperimentOverdue
        expr: max(island_intake_experiments_oldest_overdue_seconds) > 2 * 86400
        for: 1h
        labels:
          severity: warning
          platform_machinery: "true"
          triage: none
        annotations:
          summary: An intake experiment is still open more than 2 days past its bound — its verdict was not written
          description: 'An issue labelled experiment/open is still undecided two days after its window ended. The scheduled island-intake CronWorkflow (ns agent-coordinator) reads every such issue in its `experiments` step, before the sittings. Check that step''s log in the newest island-intake-* workflow (a Prometheus or GitHub read that failed, a GitHub write or a report upload that failed — the issue keeps experiment/open until one run finishes it) and read by hand: bash islands/intake/scripts/experiment-read.sh --dry-run. Reader: islands/intake/scripts/experiment-read.sh.'
      - alert: IntakeExperimentReadStale
        expr: (time() - max(max_over_time(island_intake_experiments_last_run_timestamp_seconds[8d]))) > 2 * 86400
        for: 6h
        labels:
          severity: warning
          platform_machinery: "true"
          triage: none
        annotations:
          summary: The intake experiment read has not run for more than 2 days — open experiments are not being decided
          description: 'The daily 05:00Z island-intake CronWorkflow (ns agent-coordinator) runs the experiment read as its first step; no run has pushed island_intake_experiments_last_run_timestamp_seconds in over 2 days. Check: argo -n agent-coordinator cron get island-intake and the `experiments` step of the newest island-intake-* workflow (a clone or devbox install that failed, a pod that never started). Reader: islands/intake/scripts/experiment-read.sh.'
